    Question: Harper drinks a 1/2 bottle of mineral water per day. She buys the mineral water by the case at a big box store. They come 24 bottles to a case and are currently on sale for $12.00. If she wants to buy enough cases to last her 240 days, how much will she spend? Think step by step. Answer:Harper drinks 1/2 bottle of mineral water per day, so she needs 240 days x 1/2 bottle/day = 120 bottles of mineral water. She buys the mineral water by the case, so she needs 120 bottles / 24 bottles/case = 5 cases. At $12.00 per case, she will spend 5 cases x $12.00/case = $60.00. #### 60 The answer is: 60

