    Question: Philip has a farm with animals. He has 20 cows, 50% more ducks. Philip also has as many pigs as one-fifth of ducks and cows in total. How many animals does Philip have on his farm? Think step by step. Answer:Philip has 20 cows. He has 50% more ducks, which means he has 20 * 0.5 = 10 more ducks. So he has a total of 20 + 10 = 30 ducks. Philip has as many pigs as one-fifth of ducks and cows in total, which means he has (1/5) * (30 + 20) = 10 pigs. Therefore, Philip has a total of 30 ducks + 20 cows + 10 pigs = 60 animals on his farm. #### 60 The answer is: 60

